  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe running post-merge gate finishes when more merges arrive.\nSet `cancel-in-progress: false` and update the queue comment.\nKeep the existing concurrency group.\n\nNeeds maintainer: changes .github/workflows/post-merge.yml (one line).\n\n## Cause\n\nEach new merge cancelled the running gate.\nA merge batch could leave only its last commit with a complete result.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `post_merge_preserves_running_gate` failed before the fix and passed after the fix.\n- Mutation: restore the workflow from upstream/main. The pin failed. Restore the fix. The pin passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff contains no changed `.nc` or `.cl` files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nAn actual merge batch must confirm the Actions queue behaviour after merge.\nThis draft does not start a workflow run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1738 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes the runner labels in the gate and report jobs.\nThis PR changes the top-level concurrency setting and its comment.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: low\n\nChangelog: Let a running post-merge gate finish when later merges arrive.\n\nFixes #1922\n",
